<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:54Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Thousands of Indians march to Supreme Court to oust election chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:613c64395086f8477aca13995ca5d83cfd10c6be2aa2f8648bad87a73ce115c2</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:23:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief--cfcf565f6afb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief" /><summary type="html">Protesters in New Delhi continue to take to the streets demanding the country's top election commissioner resign. Frustrations have been mounting after an investigation in a leading newspaper revealed concerns had been raised within the body, over the revision of voter lists. Delano D'Souza reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>India's opposition leader marches with thousands against election chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a052ce4ccd43973251cb1411e65ec713efe2269da308f3c93b8fc5d32dbb1ff2</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:14:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/india-s-opposition-leader-marches-with-thousands-against-election-chief--11dd429412fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/india-s-opposition-leader-marches-with-thousands-against-election-chief" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties and supporters of the so-called "cockroach" youth movement marched towards the country's Supreme Court on Monday, in the latest show of outrage against the recent removal of millions of names from voters lists. Critics say the move is likely to benefit Prime Minister Narendra Modi's ruling party – and are demanding India's election chief step down over what they describe as misconduct. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in New Delhi, Navodita Kumari.</summary></entry><entry><title>Five people missing as fresh flash floods hit central Nepal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0258f5846cec6de3ab2ec99ee705e0b6710bc094d5febb0c8094b34df6aa4ed7</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:43:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-five-people-missing-as-fresh-flash-floods-hit-central-nepal--2d9a2373d2a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-five-people-missing-as-fresh-flash-floods-hit-central-nepal" /><summary type="html">Nepali rescuers searched for five missing people on Monday, a day after new flash floods swept away more than 200 houses and five bridges along the Budhi Gandaki River. The country is still recovering from devastating floods, triggered by a mountain glacial collapse on August 26, which killed more than 1,400 people and left over 5,000 missing.</summary></entry><entry><title>Striking images show new flash floods hitting central Nepal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9eded444da874e3986c142f8c5815711ac258168a9f34a7280d9a4c83a44c66</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:14:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/striking-images-show-new-flash-floods-hitting-central-nepal--99e18aa6713c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/striking-images-show-new-flash-floods-hitting-central-nepal" /><summary type="html">Striking new images show new flash floods hitting central Nepal. This comes only six weeks after another disaster there left more than 1,400 dead and 5,000 missing. According to an initial assessment by the Nepalese authorities, at least five people are now missing. Elitsa Gadeva and France 2 have the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Illegal detentions' in India, as protesters allege foul play at Electoral Commission</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e107adfc9b9081e18c39e68a24c6d4a1326ed58f162027f4da572767c82c38b</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:51:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261012-illegal-detentions-in-india-as-protesters-allege-foul-play-at-electoral-commission--04511ed70d4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261012-illegal-detentions-in-india-as-protesters-allege-foul-play-at-electoral-commission" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, October 12: Widespread protests in India are met with detentions judged "illegal" by the country's Supreme Court. But first: Lebanese papers report as Hezbollah prepares for a new regional flare-up. Finally, Citroën hopes to win hearts and minds with an electric reboot of the vintage Deux Chevaux model.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Opposition leaders and journalists allege police abuses as fresh protests break out in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf54579575606c375a67d9e2684931161ec2360fc0d66d68ad6d56bc57e63d28</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T04:33:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-opposition-leaders-and-journalists-allege-police-abuses-as-fresh-protests-break-out-in-indi--008b7975f167.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-opposition-leaders-and-journalists-allege-police-abuses-as-fresh-protests-break-out-in-india" /><summary type="html">Indian opposition politicians and journalists alleged that police had been heavy-handed in cracking down in protests that swept New Delhi over the weekend in response to a nationwide voter roll revision that critics say disproportionately affects Muslim and other minority voters. Opposition leader Rahul Gandhi called for a fresh march to the nation's Supreme Court Monday.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Melbourne Islamic leader denies links to suspected FlyDubai hijacker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20a7bce2cacebe76e8757b2db22646603cd00fa41b9eca07db6a7d3c4189cb53</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T03:49:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-melbourne-man-linked-to-suspected-flydubai-hijacker-condemns-false-accusations--a41bc8875157.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-melbourne-man-linked-to-suspected-flydubai-hijacker-condemns-false-accusations" /><summary type="html">Abu Hamza, whose Melbourne-based Islamic community centre was linked by Emirati prosecutors to the suspect in the attempted hijacking of an Israel-bound passenger jet, publicly dismissed "false accusations" against him on Monday. While prosecutors alleged that the Omani co-pilot first became radicalised while studying in Australia, neither the community centre nor Hamza are accused of any criminal wrongdoing.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires multiple ballistic missiles off east coast, Seoul says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7da4b05f5d3aaee8c4aac7cf0ebbb2ba9a8c20073ba27021880d7a81e079b799</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T01:54:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-north-korea-ballistic-missiles-sea-japan-seoul--a82c58ea609e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-north-korea-ballistic-missiles-sea-japan-seoul" /><summary type="html">North Korea fired multiple ballistic missiles off its east coast on Monday, South Korea’s military said, amid tensions over border landmine explosions that injured three South Korean soldiers last month. Seoul said the missiles were launched from Pyongyang and increased surveillance, while Japan confirmed at least one suspected ballistic missile.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India court orders release of 'cockroach' movement leaders after detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4a1e3635538928d92f7d81ed8236d245f5f4ba400cfca3dab5c5bd501619a86</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T05:45:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261011-india-court-orders-release-of-cockroach-movement-leaders-after-detention--14ab15b3b7ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261011-india-court-orders-release-of-cockroach-movement-leaders-after-detention" /><summary type="html">An Indian court ordered the release of three leaders of the viral "cockroach" youth movement on Sunday, a day after their detention ahead of protests over alleged irregularities in voter-roll revisions. Upon his release, founder Abhijeet Dipke called Narendra Modi an "embarassment to India" in a social media post.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India detains 'cockroach' leaders ahead of election protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f58d37f6263d51c2b68fef9ae52514161250a2ef8ef1885d29081b7c538b91a3</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T09:18:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-india-detains-cockroach-leaders-ahead-of-election-protest--da3c1675b34a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-india-detains-cockroach-leaders-ahead-of-election-protest" /><summary type="html">Indian police detained the head of the satirical "cockroach" online movement on Saturday, the group said, ahead of a major protest against the Election Commission that triggered strict security measures. Our correspondent Navodita Kumari tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Indian police crack down on 'cockroach' movement protest in New Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d83569ce3f0619527ec14058f547ce4deaff0166e40b0da49452150ac757305b</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T06:37:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261010-india-s-cockroach-movement-chief-detained-ahead-of-major-protest--c11b066f94fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261010-india-s-cockroach-movement-chief-detained-ahead-of-major-protest" /><summary type="html">India's "cockroach" youth movement said Saturday that police had detained the group's leaders as well as "more than 15,000" protesters attempting to stage a major demonstration in the capital against the country's election commissioner following allegations of misconduct during voter-roll revisions.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India protests grow over Election Commission mistrust</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:223de19bccf89c3ae63227a6fff9a6197bc4fdc877e9df1c88ed8a8099c86f85</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:08:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261009-india-protests-grow-over-election-commission-mistrust--fe5514facbb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261009-india-protests-grow-over-election-commission-mistrust" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Access Asia, we find out why multiple protests have broken out in India after an investigation by The Indian Express raised concerns about the integrity of the country's Election Commission. Journalist Faye D'Souza joins us to unpack how Narendra Modi's government is facing mounting pressure from the political opposition and the Gen Z-led Cockroach Janta Party. She also discusses the wider sense of discontent in India.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>India's dowry curse: Outlawed practice remains deeply entrenched</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:438eaff6f6fd445f3a461d5346f08a0a28d92e2c2f1d8e02413f8d8068f00650</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:19:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261009-india-dowry-curse-outlawed-practice-remains-deeply-entrenched--18ff855ec4f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261009-india-dowry-curse-outlawed-practice-remains-deeply-entrenched" /><summary type="html">India recorded 5,737 dowry-linked deaths in 2024, an average of around 16 women a day. Despite being outlawed more than six decades ago, the practice of dowry – the transfer or money or valuables from a bride's family when she gets married – remains deeply entrenched across Indian society. Our correspondents report.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>China's evolving funeral practices: From traditional burials to cremation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17dcb9ff1a75f02c626404630ff61b1bf89fbceb6d526c336dfa6ef777a8279c</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:39:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261007-china-s-evolving-funeral-practices-from-traditional-burials-to-cremation--52813773e1c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261007-china-s-evolving-funeral-practices-from-traditional-burials-to-cremation" /><summary type="html">This year, China released new rules for funeral practices. The government is putting an emphasis on affordable and environmentally friendly funeral services. It's part of a decades-long reform to promote cremation. But in a country where burials are deeply rooted in local traditions, how are these attempts to modernise funerals being perceived? FRANCE 24's Yena Lee reports.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>ICC unseals arrest warrants for Taliban education ministers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba132470d0c6d933ab9e72fee7599d30be086ee3f51745451f4fd5d58ecdfca0</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T16:16:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261005-icc-unseals-arrest-warrants-for-taliban-education-ministers--eef86bb29f9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261005-icc-unseals-arrest-warrants-for-taliban-education-ministers" /><summary type="html">The International Criminal Court on Monday unsealed warrants for Afghan Education Minister Habibullah Agha, and Higher Education Minister Neda Mohammad Nadeem, accusing two senior Taliban officials of crimes against humanity for denying Afghanistan's women and girls over 12 their rights to an education.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Indian police detain demonstrators as protests over voter roll revision intensify</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d27010f9662489d6c6d176a93622f8065534413f59a8f8facb95007ce7bfe6b7</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T11:04:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-ndian-police-detain-demonstrators-as-protests-over-voter-roll-revision-intensify--4a3d03cb8d05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-ndian-police-detain-demonstrators-as-protests-over-voter-roll-revision-intensify" /><summary type="html">Thousands of youth protesters and opposition supporters rallied in Delhi and Mumbai on Sunday to demand the resignation of India's election commission chief over changes to ​voter rolls as ‌police detained some demonstrators for a third day.</summary></entry><entry><title>North Korea launches ballistic missile as tensions with Seoul grow over border mine blasts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb9c98ed8aa6201e0182160a04cc3c1f7ba5026e0dbd698b6af9fbf9757cb505</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T02:40:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261003-north-korea-fires-ballistic-missile-after-seoul-s-apology-demand--31f42c33e2e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261003-north-korea-fires-ballistic-missile-after-seoul-s-apology-demand" /><summary type="html">North Korea launched a ballistic missile Saturday morning from the Wonsan area on its east coast into the Sea of Japan, according to South Korea's military. The launch comes amid renewed tensions between Pyongyang and Seoul, with the latter demanding an apology for a blast that wounded three South Korean soldiers inside the Demilitarized Zone last month.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'Make our streets safer!' Mass women's protests sweep India over sexual violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd2a31df850e09ae913a1d701dec2172a5d57f0a6facf63b5e811441da535d42</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:57:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261002-make-our-streets-safer-mass-women-s-protests-sweep-india-over-sexual-violence--825117eadd3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261002-make-our-streets-safer-mass-women-s-protests-sweep-india-over-sexual-violence" /><summary type="html">In India, thousands of women have been taking to the streets calling for better protection of female students, following the suspected gang rape of a 17-year-old girl. The alleged incident in an upscale neighbourhood of New Delhi prompted authorities to beef up protective measures, but the women say limiting their access to public spaces is not the answer.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Thailand floods: At least 8 die, thousands move to shelters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6044bbc85687f4e3a2fd2a6fa7eee9356283d53b447d0a945af373a6239137f</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T11:20:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-thailand-floods-at-least-8-die-thousands-move-to-shelters--915a2d7132c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-thailand-floods-at-least-8-die-thousands-move-to-shelters" /><summary type="html">Rain eased in Thailand ’s capital on Sunday, but flooding persisted in several low-lying areas, with thousands forced to move into temporary shelters. At least eight people were reported killed in the past 10 days nationwide.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands evacuated amid Bangkok floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:037e5e0b7b9f06e8897f3ff2c06705a903c4f7cd0304986dd5d04ff8892311f5</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-evacuated-amid-bangkok-floods--f805440afd9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-evacuated-amid-bangkok-floods" /><summary type="html">Rain is easing in Thailand’s capital, but flooding continues in several low-lying areas. Thousands of people have been forced into temporary shelters after the government declared Bangkok a disaster zone on Saturday. At least eight people have died over the past 10 days as heavy rains caused widespread disruption. Juliette Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>A month after, thousands are still missing and families face a long recovery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c00b089ef34fd5240a99dd4de5f7673484415ad7cf1c1983f807081a008984df</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T09:40:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-month-after-thousands-are-still-missing-and-families-face-a-long-recovery--547bee35856b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-month-after-thousands-are-still-missing-and-families-face-a-long-recovery" /><summary type="html">A month after Nepal’s floods, thousands are still missing and families face a long recovery.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bangkok declares flood disaster after massive 48-hour downpour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c7847d4fe5e57572d8173bf7d3e1968f478e8d1847985b148f5985e24615807</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T04:40:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260926-bangkok-declares-flood-disaster-after-massive-48h-downpour--629faecd1f1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260926-bangkok-declares-flood-disaster-after-massive-48h-downpour" /><summary type="html">Thailand’s capital Bangkok declared a flood disaster on Saturday after more than 300 millimetres of rain in less than 48 hours, leaving canals overflowing and streets submerged. “It’s like at my waist level now,” a local said. The governor has urged people not to panic, saying the situation is stabilising.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Fatalities on Indian roads: One death reported every three minutes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d415340827440057e2dd716579d142a1bb5a4a1b407d3125ef1b8d2f57a4476</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:33:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260925-fatalities-on-indian-roads-one-death-reported-every-three-minutes--b0b4970ad80e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260925-fatalities-on-indian-roads-one-death-reported-every-three-minutes" /><summary type="html">India has the second-largest road network in the world, spanning over 6 million kilometres. But these roads are silent killers, with one death reported every three minutes. Every day, headlines are filled with horror stories: drunk drivers mowing people down, school buses hit by speeding trucks killing children, buses with dozens of passengers plunging into gorges.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Journalism and resistance under Taliban rule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:625c80b4e9c3dcf6618fa058ff8f8c1ddc4e54183af7765fa52344c939e11d26</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T10:21:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260925-journalism-and-resistance-under-taliban-rule--1976c788e5fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260925-journalism-and-resistance-under-taliban-rule" /><summary type="html">In this edition, we focus on Afghanistan, which recently marked the fifth anniversary of the Taliban's return to power. Since then, the exclusion of women and girls has become normalised, with the government systematically dismantling the rights of more than half the country's population.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal’s catastrophic floods were ‘warning to the world', PM Shah tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:580676e335c6df50e4769d973b90dabb5c319799485000543979e482e8931ca0</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T01:42:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260925-nepal-floods-warning-world-pm-shah-un--2fd13a540ae2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260925-nepal-floods-warning-world-pm-shah-un" /><summary type="html">Nepal’s Prime Minister Balendra Shah said on Thursday that last month’s catastrophic floods were a “warning to the world” of growing climate risks in the Himalayas. He said warming was melting glaciers and permafrost and urged international support to help Nepal adapt to threats it could not face alone.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'Trump views US-China relations as a personal friendship: Xi views US as an adversary to be managed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d97f0b7711a099704e3293feed9e6900d4738905df78148eb809f2b49c37591a</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed--29eaaa0e21d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Henrietta Levin, Senior Fellow with the Freeman Chair in China Studies at the Center for Strategic and International Studies in Washington. The US remains a powerful actor in its relationship with China. But power on paper is not the same thing as leverage at the negotiating table. Levin warns that President Trump’s highly personalized approach to Xi Jinping offers Beijing opportunities that China can easily exploit. Xi does not approach the relationship in the same way. Au contraire, he sees the United States as an adversary to be managed while China pursues its domestic priorities and strategic objectives in Asia, including on Taiwan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Taiwan: Home of semiconductor giants at the centre of AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2448617ba74257fe43746c2e93cfcec96a0333b71aac92d91d1fa27359d87c87</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race--f4a0e175142c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race" /><summary type="html">The topic of artificial intelligence looms large as Chinese President Xi Jinping begins his highly anticipated state visit to Washington. The fate of Taiwan – coveted by its larger neighbour, China – will also be on the table. It's the global leader in superconductor research and development. These powerful chips can be found in smartphones, computers, and above all in AI development. Our France 2 colleagues take a rare look inside one of Taiwan's state-of-the-art laboratories.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan launches air strikes in Afghanistan, killing civilians, Taliban says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:400097dbd0e7279ec6eecc3c1da194c218f144627b0ecd3ca82b27fa06e39b82</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T08:53:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260924-pakistan-launches-air-strikes-in-afghanistan-killing-civilians-taliban-says--7caa8e352d5c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260924-pakistan-launches-air-strikes-in-afghanistan-killing-civilians-taliban-says" /><summary type="html">Pakistan launched air strikes Thursday on 10 sites in Afghanistan in what Islamabad said was a retaliation for a drone attack by Afghanistan's Taliban forces on a border post. A Taliban government spokesman denied the allegation and said Pakistan's latest strikes killed four civilians in Afghanistan's southern and eastern provinces.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>China cracks down on scam centres in neighbouring Myanmar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4348e6ac83d3229fa0c486abb3455599bec7ebaa0e3a1132978273c6aaaf4305</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:01:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260923-china-cracks-down-on-scam-centres-in-neighbouring-myanmar--6eaea5ec0493.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260923-china-cracks-down-on-scam-centres-in-neighbouring-myanmar" /><summary type="html">In Southeast Asia, hundreds of thousands of people working in fraud centres are scamming people across the world. US authorities suggest the fraudsters are responsible for scams worth almost $10 billion a year against US nationals alone. Victims in Europe, the UK and China have also been targeted. Human rights groups further warn that those working in the centres are often themselves victims of human trafficking – forced to work as slaves.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: 15 convicted over Easter bombings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b90596e1b728ba7257c19d1681b6d8540a73c1788c6cbdb4b335a399821a9692</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:36:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sri-lanka-15-convicted-over-easter-bombings--22aa604a66ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sri-lanka-15-convicted-over-easter-bombings" /><summary type="html">Sri Lanka’s 2019 Easter bombings, one of the deadliest attacks in the country’s history, killed more than 260 people. After a trial lasting nearly five years, 15 men have now been convicted over the attacks, which were inspired by the Islamic State group. All those convicted are members of Sri Lanka’s Muslim minority. Ellen Gainsford reports on their sentences.</summary></entry></feed>
